+"""One-user MTP generation that keeps its caches between requests (for a chat or a local server).
+
+A chat or a coding harness sends the whole conversation again on each turn. The new prompt then starts with the
+previous prompt. After each prompt prefill the session records a checkpoint: the token ids, the length of each
+K/V cache (attention and MTP head) and the recurrent (GDN) state arrays. MLX arrays do not change in place, so the
+checkpoint holds references and copies nothing. When the next prompt starts with the checkpoint tokens, the session
+trims the K/V caches back to the checkpoint, sets the recurrent state again and reads only the new tokens. Any other
+prompt starts from empty caches.
