+the first ``snapshots`` chunk ends at or below ``snapshot_max`` tokens. A later prompt that leaves the conversation
+inside the prompt (an edited turn, a client that drops the reasoning) restores the longest snapshot that is its prefix
+and reads from there. When a prompt that shares no snapshot arrives (a new conversation, or a short side request
+such as a title request of a coding agent), the session first copies the K/V of the longest snapshot out of the old
+conversation ("pinned prefix"). A next conversation with the same system prompt and tools then reads only the part
+after it. Cost on Qwen3.8-27B with the fp16 GDN state: about 78 MB per snapshot (48 GDN layers) and 68 KiB per
